Strategy for me is not go for the racket with a monk. Barehanded 
Samarai,Monk,Barbarian and Caveman classes don't need to do the 
racket to survive mid level. Their skills give them just enough 
fighting power. (sam and monk more than enough.)

Keep your pet just in case. If you really want to do the racket, wear 
some armor on the way down. That way you can't hit the broadside of a 
barn with just walking. You can still kick in emergencies. 

Once your barehanded skill is high enough, wear some good body armor. 
(your choices are limited if you are a spellcaster.) Kick things in 
combat and you get past the -20 to hit penalty. Just remember to 
never go around burdened. 

If you get an early wand of wishing, do wish for DSM. You can start 
kicking right away with this character. 

Good luck  

